arm64-darwin  cxx1 keeps a cleanup for the guarded initialisation of `once` - `___cxa_guard_abort` and the `__Unwind_Resume` it ends in - because since 1.26 a static local whose initialiser throws is built again on the next call ([stmt.dcl]/4), where clang sees that binding `*p` cannot throw and emits neither. Both are legal; cxx1 is the conservative side, as conditional-class.nonames records for a cleanup region. The file-scope references agree.
